---
alwaysApply: true
---

This project uses OpenPlanet AngelScript. Apply strict protections:

Do not rename, reorder, remove, or wrap any of the following:
UI::* functions, Render() functions, plugin entry points, window/component classes, or any function that pushes or pops UI state.

Treat UI::* as commands interacting with a strict stack. Any Push* must have a corresponding Pop* in the same control path. Never move them. Never combine or split them. Never insert early returns between them.

Do not modify the order of Begin/End pairs, Child/EndChild, BeginTabBar/EndTabBar, BeginTabItem/EndTabItem, BeginDisabled/EndDisabled. Never nest them differently.

Do not introduce C++ patterns such as references, templates, smart pointers, RAII, or destructors. AngelScript does not support them.

Functions called by the engine (including Render, OnSettingsChanged, Main, and window component methods) must preserve their signatures exactly.

Do not change the type signatures of arrays, dictionaries, or engine objects. Do not convert data structures to STL-like forms.

Do not optimize or “clean up” control flow around UI blocks. Maintain the original ordering.

When reorganizing code, isolate mechanical edits (naming, extraction, file splitting) from UI logic. Never touch UI stack calls.

If uncertain about safety, leave the original structure unchanged.
